pyra-settings (0.15) trixie; urgency=medium

  * GUI: Performance page: a top CPU speed (No limit, or one of the
    kernel's steps from 1400 down to 250 MHz) and the top speed the thermal
    daemon has set now. Needs pyra-hacks 0.38+pyra5 or later, whose thermal
    daemon reads the ceiling within 2 s; with an older one the page says so.
  * Helper: set-cpu-max writes CPU_MAX_MHZ to /etc/default/pyra-thermal, or
    deletes the file for no limit. Purge removes the file only if the helper
    wrote it.
  * Packaging: Recommends pyra-hacks (>= 0.38+pyra5).

 -- pyra-settings maintainers <pyra-settings@example.invalid>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

pyra-settings (0.14) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Packaging: pyra-hacks and pyra-backlight are Recommends, not Depends, so
    the package installs without them. The Volume wheel and Display pages
    each say when their daemon is missing.
  * Wake: no fallback for kernels without patch 0053, which every image
    has. Without it the wake rows show as unreadable and the helper
    writes nothing. Not yet tested on the Pyra on a 0053 kernel: the
    per-button wake rows have never run on the device, and lid wake was
    only tested through the old fallback.
  * Packaging: the description covers every page.
  * Release builds on GitHub from a v* tag.

 -- pyra-settings maintainers <pyra-settings@example.invalid>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

